comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T16:42:33.856Z","harness:codex","Implementation start: active in the shared runtime-capability-contracts bundle. Duplicate check covered all 2,136 tracker items and live GitHub reports; this item owns a distinct acceptance facet and will share exact-head verification with the related active items."
  "2026-07-27T18:19:07.707Z","harness:codex","Evidence: core/standard/full/custom profiles validate exact names and workspace extension actions. The default core payload is 34,828 bytes (13 tools), below the prior 42,359-byte budget; detailed schema descriptions are removed only from core input schemas while full remains lossless. Token-surface and profile tests pass."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-13T09:32:19.589Z",maintainer-agent,"Rationale evidence: June 2026 tool-selection study (arxiv 2606.30317) found substantial accuracy degradation as available tool count grows (threshold varies by model); Task Master independently ships core/standard/full MCP tiers with explicit token budgets for the same reason. Pair with MCP resources+prompts (owned by pm-z3ez) so stable reference context does not need to be a tool. Selection quality is an agent-acquisition lever, not just a token saving — a smaller, sharper surface makes agents pick pm tools correctly more often."
  "2026-07-15T19:27:28.263Z",maintainer-agent,"Re-measurement 2026-07-15 (review pass #89, scripts/measure-agent-token-surface.mjs): MCP tools/list 33,314 B / 8,329 tokens / 28 tools — up from the pm-a22j baseline 32,979 B (2026-07-11). Every session with the MCP server attached pays ~8.3k tokens before the first call, and each new tool/flag grows it; the core/standard/full profile tiers this item owns are the structural fix. Companion figure: full-format single-item surface is 539,946 B (~135k tokens) vs summary_json 4,426 B — the 122x spread shows how much the profile/format choices matter for agent context budgets."
  "2026-07-18T05:42:19.706Z",maintainer-agent,"Surface re-measurement 2026-07-18 (scripts/measure-agent-token-surface.mjs, post-PR#580/#581): MCP tools/list now 29 tools / 34,975 B / ~8,744 tokens — up from the pm-a22j baseline of 28 tools / 32,979 B / ~8.2k tokens (pm_graph added; growth passed the token-budget gate deliberately). Every new first-class tool now costs every agent cold start ~+500 tokens, which strengthens the case for the profile tiers this item owns: a graph-heavy agent needs pm_graph but a triage agent never does. Use these numbers as the before-figure when profiles land."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T18:19:08.471Z","harness:codex","Keep default MCP schemas structurally complete but description-compact; hosts already receive tool descriptions, and stripping nested descriptions reduced tools/list from 69,974 to 34,828 bytes without weakening validation."
